[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from the branch/index structure of `c_src/src/lib.c`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Public entry points (full set, lowest level included)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/include/lib.h` declares exactly one function and it *is* the lowest-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entry point — there are no convenience wrappers, no init/teardown, no opaque
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m context object and no setter functions:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unsigned hdr_bitrate(const uint8_t *h);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the entry-point axis has a single value, and every row below drives that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m function directly through the `.so` export.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The body contains no `if` / `switch` / `#ifdef`, so there are no runtime
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m option/mode/flag axes. All branching is *data* branching through three index
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m expressions:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | expression in C | distinct values | effect |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|-----------------|-----------------|--------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | A. version bit | `!!((h[1]) & 0x8)` → `i` | 2 (`0`, `1`) | selects `halfrate[i]`, i.e. flat offset `+0` or `+45` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | B. layer field | `(((h[1]) >> 1) & 3) - 1` → `j` | 4 (`-1`, `0`, `1`, `2`) | selects the row, `+15*j`; value `-1` (layer field `0b00`) escapes the declared bounds |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C. bitrate nibble | `((h[2]) >> 4)` → `k` | 16 (`0..15`) | byte within the row; value `15` escapes the declared 15-byte row |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | D. ignored input bits | — | — | `h[0]`, `h[1] & 0x01`, `h[1] & 0xF0`, `h[2] & 0x0F`, and `h[3]`+ are **never read**; changing them must not change the result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E. buffer shape | — | — | no length parameter; C touches exactly `h[1]` and `h[2]`, so buffer length ≥ 3, pointer alignment, and offset-into-a-larger-buffer must all be irrelevant |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pruning C: the code treats `k` differently for every value, but three classes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m carry distinct *meaning* and distinct in/out-of-bounds behaviour: `k = 0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (the "free" bitrate slot, always table value `0`), `k = 1..14` (in-range table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entries), `k = 15` (the "bad" index, one past the row). Rows are the cross
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m product A × B × {k=0, k∈1..14, k=15} = 2 × 4 × 3 = 24, plus rows for axes D and E.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** (fixed seed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0x5DEECE66D`, SplitMix64) over the free bits of that configuration — the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ignored bits of `h[1]`/`h[2]`, all of `h[0]`/`h[3..]`, buffer length, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m buffer offset — and over the full `k` sub-range where the row spans one.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Cargo feature combinations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` section**, so the complete
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m feature-combination set is the single default configuration (equivalently
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `--no-default-features`, which is identical here). Both are run; see the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `run_all.sh` output recorded in the completion gate.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C01 | `hdr_bitrate` | A: `i=0` (`h[1]&0x8 == 0`); B: layer field `0b00` ⇒ `j=-1`; C: `k=0` ⇒ flat offset `-15`, read before the table | [x] |
